    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1333">

                <pb facs="1082" n="1072" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1072"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.7146/3–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-23T12:00:00+08:00">March 23,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 23—1:58 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>462. ReContel 444, March 21. Requested information was handed inspector 1100
                    hours today under cover unaddressed memo signed by <pb facs="1083" n="1073"
                        xml:id="pg1073"/> me as Consul General. As regards radio station, it was
                    confirmed Consulate General possessed one “which was of course established
                    according to a pertinent agreement”.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking, Shanghai and Canton.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
